WEBVTT

00:24.541 --> 00:25.501
I can see it.

00:27.961 --> 00:29.211
I'm fine.

00:36.301 --> 00:38.931
I can dodge it if I watch closely.

00:39.011 --> 00:42.561
If I don't get hit,
it doesn't matter what weapon he uses.

00:49.321 --> 00:50.651
Yeah!

00:53.741 --> 00:55.151
Nice, kid!

00:55.241 --> 00:56.321
You can do it!

00:56.411 --> 00:58.411
That kid's pretty good!

00:58.491 --> 01:00.661
He was able to hit the captain.

01:00.741 --> 01:02.911
Quick guys like him are tough!

01:03.001 --> 01:05.621
This could turn out to be a good fight!

01:06.671 --> 01:10.501
Damn! I can't cut him.
He's wearing chain mail underneath.

01:10.591 --> 01:12.091
Too bad, I liked these.

01:13.961 --> 01:17.641
So, you're not afraid of my ax?

01:17.721 --> 01:22.471
You have a lot of guts. You're just like Thors.

01:24.431 --> 01:27.981
You big bastard. Who are you to my father?

01:29.981 --> 01:35.611
He didn't tell you? That's so cold of him.

01:35.691 --> 01:38.911
I heard he's descended from a jarl.
He was of noble origin.

01:39.911 --> 01:42.951
Helga's the one from a family of jarls.

01:43.041 --> 01:45.871
Thors rose through the ranks
because of his skill with the sword.

01:45.961 --> 01:47.121
What?

01:47.211 --> 01:49.381
Do you want to know more?

01:50.791 --> 01:51.631
Do you?

01:54.301 --> 01:56.301
If you want me to tell you,

01:56.381 --> 01:59.891
you'll have to entertain me some more.

01:59.971 --> 02:01.261
All right, Thorfinn?

02:03.971 --> 02:06.271
I can entertain you.

02:07.271 --> 02:10.811
But it's going to be hard holding back enough
to make sure you can still talk.

02:14.361 --> 02:16.401
Do you know what you're saying, kid?

02:16.491 --> 02:17.781
My stomach hurts!

02:17.861 --> 02:19.451
Holding back on the captain? You?

02:19.531 --> 02:21.451
Go easy on us!

02:21.531 --> 02:22.991
You're an idiot! You're an idiot!

02:28.331 --> 02:30.211
Was that funny?

02:30.291 --> 02:33.291
I consider Thorfinn to be a warrior.

02:33.381 --> 02:34.551
Don't laugh!

02:39.591 --> 02:42.931
Thors was stronger than me.

02:43.011 --> 02:46.971
Prove to me that you really are Thors' child,

02:47.061 --> 02:48.351
Thorfinn!

04:29.951 --> 04:33.331
That stupid kid. He came back here to die.

04:35.121 --> 04:37.251
What happened to the prince?

04:39.251 --> 04:41.301
Hey! Over there! Go!

04:42.301 --> 04:44.171
Hold down his leg!

04:44.261 --> 04:45.431
OUT OF THE CRADLE

04:45.511 --> 04:46.591
Do the same over there!

04:46.681 --> 04:50.061
I can hear the sound the of battle nearby.

04:51.351 --> 04:53.771
Stop it already!

04:55.731 --> 04:57.901
Don't you have anything better to do?

04:59.651 --> 05:01.281
Be quiet!

05:02.281 --> 05:03.991
I don't want to open my eyes.

05:05.031 --> 05:06.661
I want to stay asleep...

05:07.911 --> 05:10.581
like this... forever.

05:12.041 --> 05:17.961
Your Highness... Your Highness...
Your Highness Canute.

05:30.851 --> 05:33.471
Ragnar! You're still alive--

05:42.481 --> 05:47.111
This is a dream, isn't it, Ragnar?

05:49.161 --> 05:52.991
Yes. I came to say goodbye.

05:57.161 --> 06:00.461
Are you going? You'll leave me behind?

06:03.631 --> 06:08.591
Are you telling me to live alone in a world like this?

06:09.801 --> 06:11.601
Do you think I can survive?

06:18.521 --> 06:19.901
I...

06:20.981 --> 06:25.651
failed as the person tasked
with your education.

06:26.651 --> 06:31.911
I was supposed to raise you as a jarl.
But I raised you as a normal child,

06:31.991 --> 06:37.451
like a farmer would raise his own child.

06:38.541 --> 06:44.671
Even though I knew that's not what the king wanted.
Please forgive me.

06:47.631 --> 06:54.301
What's wrong with that? You understood my feelings
better than my father, the king!

07:00.851 --> 07:04.311
I never wanted to be born into the royal family.

07:07.481 --> 07:08.901
If I had been...

07:09.991 --> 07:14.241
If I had been born as your son,

07:14.321 --> 07:17.791
everything would have been better.

07:21.251 --> 07:22.791
Your Highness.

07:22.881 --> 07:26.501
I'm so happy, Your Highness.

07:26.591 --> 07:31.221
Don't go. I love you.

07:44.901 --> 07:48.731
There are some things that you only realize
once you've experienced a loss.

07:48.821 --> 07:52.241
You've noticed already.

07:52.321 --> 07:53.161
Ragnar...

07:53.241 --> 07:55.371
I'm just a dream.

07:55.451 --> 07:56.281
Wait...

07:56.371 --> 07:58.661
The time for you to awake has come.

07:58.741 --> 08:01.121
No... Ragnar!

08:01.211 --> 08:02.461
Come back!

08:03.671 --> 08:04.501
Come back!

08:07.421 --> 08:10.801
I wish you well, Your Highness.

08:16.091 --> 08:17.181
Ragnar...

08:35.861 --> 08:38.581
Don't be afraid! Attack together!

08:46.421 --> 08:49.501
Are you hurt anywhere?

08:53.591 --> 08:58.351
Those men are fighting over you.

08:58.431 --> 09:01.181
The winner is going to take you.

09:04.181 --> 09:07.981
You're a priest. Aren't you going
to stop them from fighting?

09:09.021 --> 09:14.571
Is there a way to stop them? It's better
to let those who wish to die, die.

09:23.581 --> 09:24.911
I had a dream.

09:26.041 --> 09:27.541
It was a dream about Ragnar.

09:28.961 --> 09:30.501
He said goodbye.

09:31.631 --> 09:33.711
He was a faithful man, even in death.

09:38.221 --> 09:39.931
In this world...

09:41.011 --> 09:44.061
there's no one who loves me anymore.

09:47.351 --> 09:52.401
You've found enlightenment. But you're wrong.

09:53.821 --> 09:58.071
Was the emotion that Ragnar felt towards you love?

09:59.531 --> 10:02.121
In order to keep you safe,

10:02.201 --> 10:05.411
he watched as 62 innocent villagers were killed.

10:08.171 --> 10:09.791
Your Highness.

10:09.881 --> 10:11.291
Love...

10:11.381 --> 10:12.541
What is it?

10:16.011 --> 10:19.761
But you know, these guys weren't that good.

10:19.841 --> 10:23.311
It's not easy to find strong opponents.

10:23.391 --> 10:26.221
We'll never get to Valhalla.

10:29.351 --> 10:31.361
Is the captain's duel still going on?

10:31.441 --> 10:33.441
No way. He should have killed him instantly.

10:33.521 --> 10:35.981
Then what are they so excited about?

10:37.741 --> 10:39.031
I'll go check.

10:39.111 --> 10:40.071
Me too.

10:40.161 --> 10:41.661
Hey! What's going on?

10:43.911 --> 10:44.871
Kill him!

10:44.951 --> 10:45.791
Captain!

10:45.871 --> 10:46.911
You kid!

10:47.001 --> 10:48.161
Stop running away!

10:59.381 --> 11:00.471
Impossible!

11:00.551 --> 11:02.471
How could the captain...?

11:02.551 --> 11:06.221
He's getting beaten up by that kid!

11:06.311 --> 11:08.681
Nice, Thorfinn!

11:08.771 --> 11:13.061
I don't even have five men who'd be a match for you!

11:16.151 --> 11:18.781
It's the same chain mail as before.

11:18.861 --> 11:21.241
I should aim for tendons in his arms and legs.

11:22.241 --> 11:26.121
I tried to go after his vitals in London,
and I paid the price.

11:26.201 --> 11:28.951
I can deliver the final blow once I stop him from moving.

11:29.961 --> 11:34.881
However, I know you're strong,
but your swordsmanship

11:34.961 --> 11:37.961
is, well, only average.

11:39.211 --> 11:42.761
There's still something missing
before you achieve perfection as a warrior.

11:44.971 --> 11:48.391
If that's the case, then,
why are you having a hard time?

11:48.471 --> 11:50.021
Good point.

11:50.101 --> 11:51.941
I'm missing something, too.

11:52.021 --> 11:56.361
I thought perhaps I could learn it from you,
since you're Thors' child.

11:58.731 --> 12:01.151
Hey, Thorfinn.

12:01.241 --> 12:02.741
What do you think?

12:06.741 --> 12:08.621
What does it mean

12:09.621 --> 12:10.581
to be a true warrior?

12:18.881 --> 12:21.671
Are you asking what love is?

12:23.221 --> 12:26.471
Are you saying that Ragnar didn't love me?

12:28.051 --> 12:28.971
Yes.

12:30.641 --> 12:32.681
Then let me ask you.

12:33.731 --> 12:35.941
If what Ragnar felt wasn't love,

12:36.021 --> 12:39.231
then who can embody love correctly?

12:40.731 --> 12:42.441
He's right there.

12:43.451 --> 12:44.321
See?

12:49.411 --> 12:55.501
When he died, he became more beautiful
than anyone among the living.

12:55.581 --> 12:57.711
He's love itself.

13:00.171 --> 13:05.431
He'll never hate others or steal anymore.

13:06.721 --> 13:09.931
He was abandoned there.

13:10.011 --> 13:14.681
He's going to give his body with generosity
to the beasts and the insects.

13:16.061 --> 13:19.191
He lies exposed to the wind and the rain,

13:19.271 --> 13:22.441
but won't speak a single word in complaint.

13:25.071 --> 13:26.151
Death...

13:27.491 --> 13:30.161
perfects a person.

13:38.541 --> 13:39.381
Hey!

13:39.461 --> 13:41.211
Do it! Come on!

13:43.631 --> 13:45.091
Damn!

13:45.171 --> 13:47.091
So, you don't know?

13:47.181 --> 13:50.301
Don't worry about it.
I wasn't expecting you to know anyway.

13:51.601 --> 13:53.391
That was dirty!

13:59.231 --> 14:03.021
Are you saying that death is the essence of love?

14:05.111 --> 14:06.111
Yes.

14:07.111 --> 14:11.241
Then what is the feeling when parents
care for their children,

14:11.321 --> 14:15.871
when a husband and wife care for each other,
and when Ragnar cares about me?

14:15.951 --> 14:18.331
It's discrimination.

14:18.421 --> 14:23.131
It's no different from fawning over a king
while hitting a slave with a whip.

14:24.591 --> 14:30.591
To Ragnar, you were more important
than anyone else, Your Highness.

14:31.601 --> 14:34.811
Probably even more important than his own life.

14:37.021 --> 14:43.611
His tender feelings towards you were discrimination.

14:51.951 --> 14:53.201
I see.

14:55.491 --> 14:56.831
I'm beginning to understand.

15:00.331 --> 15:02.211
I feel like

15:02.291 --> 15:04.421
the fog has lifted.

15:10.131 --> 15:11.551
What?

15:11.641 --> 15:13.221
Come on!

15:13.301 --> 15:14.431
He's done with you!

15:15.891 --> 15:16.891
Hey...

15:25.901 --> 15:28.321
Damn... It's still too shallow.

15:33.781 --> 15:35.451
I'm beginning to understand.

15:35.531 --> 15:36.911
This snow...

15:38.661 --> 15:40.461
is love, right?

15:41.751 --> 15:43.211
That's right.

15:47.211 --> 15:48.461
The sky.

15:49.801 --> 15:51.171
The sun.

15:52.181 --> 15:54.051
The wind.

15:54.141 --> 15:54.971
The fog.

15:56.101 --> 15:57.261
The mountains.

16:02.391 --> 16:03.401
But then...

16:07.651 --> 16:08.981
I can't believe it.

16:09.981 --> 16:11.031
The world.

16:12.031 --> 16:15.411
The creation of God is so beautiful.
But then why...

16:19.081 --> 16:20.911
is there no love...

16:22.461 --> 16:23.921
in the hearts of men?

16:32.051 --> 16:35.761
They say that the reason we turned into
creatures like this

16:37.101 --> 16:40.311
is because our ancestors disobeyed God

16:40.391 --> 16:44.061
and committed a sin long ago.

16:46.021 --> 16:47.361
We were...

16:48.651 --> 16:51.571
expelled from paradise.

17:05.461 --> 17:06.291
What?

17:06.371 --> 17:07.711
Where did he go?

17:08.921 --> 17:10.751
Hey. What's that?

17:10.841 --> 17:15.131
He dampened the shock with his legs. Nice move.

17:25.311 --> 17:26.191
Over there!

17:26.271 --> 17:27.811
Wow!

17:27.901 --> 17:29.021
He must be dead now!

17:29.111 --> 17:31.111
Impressive, captain!

17:32.901 --> 17:34.151
Damn.

17:35.201 --> 17:37.611
I've lost all hope now.

18:05.771 --> 18:07.811
It looks like the battle is over.

18:09.191 --> 18:10.901
But

18:10.981 --> 18:15.321
this is no good. That man has gone insane.

18:17.031 --> 18:20.071
Your Highness. You had better run away.

18:25.201 --> 18:26.371
Sane?

18:28.001 --> 18:31.751
Is anyone sane in this world?

18:34.921 --> 18:36.301
Everyone's the same.

18:37.471 --> 18:38.801
Everyone's the same.

18:40.131 --> 18:44.181
No one knows how to love.

18:45.311 --> 18:47.271
No one knows the meaning of life.

18:47.351 --> 18:49.101
No one knows the meaning of death.

18:50.101 --> 18:52.651
No one even knows the reason they're fighting.

18:54.231 --> 18:55.321
Your Highness.

19:01.821 --> 19:04.911
I've had enough. I'm sick of it.

19:18.671 --> 19:22.551
What we lost in exchange for wisdom...

19:22.641 --> 19:26.931
The most important thing... It's something

19:27.021 --> 19:31.101
that we'll never get back as long as we live.

19:36.191 --> 19:37.651
We'll never attain it.

19:38.651 --> 19:40.321
Yet, even then...

19:40.401 --> 19:42.911
You still tell us to seek it?

19:44.161 --> 19:45.661
Father in heaven!

19:57.841 --> 19:59.921
Miserable warrior.

20:00.011 --> 20:02.011
You're the farthest from love.

20:03.091 --> 20:05.011
You, who have been expelled from paradise.

20:13.311 --> 20:18.361
Isn't there any way to end the suffering
from your punishment other than death?

20:20.861 --> 20:26.241
Are you saying that we only exist
so that we may be tested and endure?

20:26.321 --> 20:28.201
Father in heaven!

20:28.281 --> 20:32.461
This man's soul cannot be saved
through the trials you set for him!

20:55.651 --> 20:56.691
Father.

20:57.691 --> 20:59.861
I no longer seek your salvation.

21:00.861 --> 21:03.151
If you will no longer give us salvation,

21:03.241 --> 21:05.031
then, with our own hands,

21:05.111 --> 21:06.991
on this earth,

21:07.071 --> 21:08.871
we shall create our own paradise.

21:13.081 --> 21:15.291
What? Prince?

21:22.381 --> 21:23.761
Ow!

21:23.841 --> 21:25.681
Prince! Are you okay?

21:27.511 --> 21:29.641
Stop, you fools.

21:29.721 --> 21:31.931
Don't fight futile battles anymore.

21:32.021 --> 21:33.931
Futile?

21:36.771 --> 21:38.941
Your wounds are deep. Are you okay?

21:39.021 --> 21:42.821
Damn. I slipped up.

21:42.901 --> 21:46.361
Don't move. Your stomach is cut. Willibald!

21:48.411 --> 21:50.491
Treat his wounds.

21:50.581 --> 21:52.411
I'm going to catch the horses.

21:53.451 --> 21:54.951
You. Help him.

21:56.161 --> 22:00.461
Your Highness, I've seen a miracle.

22:00.541 --> 22:02.341
Be quiet and treat his wounds.

22:02.421 --> 22:06.721
Hey! Prince! Where are you going?

22:06.801 --> 22:12.061
We're going to give you to Thorkell!
Or else my buddies--

22:12.141 --> 22:14.521
I was already planning to see Thorkell.

22:15.521 --> 22:19.231
We won't be able to transport the wounded
unless we borrow their sleds.

22:19.311 --> 22:23.361
What? You're talking nonsense!

22:23.441 --> 22:27.201
Do you have any idea why I'm in
such a mess right now? You idiot!

22:27.281 --> 22:31.321
If you get captured by Thorkell,
then there will be no meaning to any of this!

22:32.741 --> 22:33.871
Meaning?

22:33.951 --> 22:35.581
Did you say meaning?

22:35.661 --> 22:37.961
The meaning of your battles?

22:41.791 --> 22:44.341
There is no meaning to a battle like this.

22:45.341 --> 22:46.841
So, don't die.

22:48.671 --> 22:51.841
Warriors. Become my vassals.

22:51.931 --> 22:56.021
I shall teach you about when you must fight,
and against whom.

22:57.311 --> 23:02.561
I shall give meaning to your battles.
To your life and death.

23:05.151 --> 23:05.981
That's what...

23:07.861 --> 23:09.361
the duty of a king is.
